      <!-- Closing -->
      <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          <strong class="text-white">Latex-ite</strong> sits where most homeowners want a driveway sealer to sit: widely stocked, straightforward to apply, and priced sensibly for the coverage it delivers. It is not the longest-lasting product on the market, and it does not claim to be.
        </p>
        <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
          Applied properly — pail stirred thoroughly, cracks filled first, surface genuinely dry, two thin coats on a warm dry day — it gives two to three solid years on a residential driveway. Applied thin over unfilled cracks on a damp surface, no sealer at this price does better.
        </p>
